course: dictionary
lesson: 9726
title: Sunday, the day after Saturday
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Sunday is a day of the week. It comes after Saturday and before Monday. Count the days on your fingers to check: Monday, Tuesday, Wednesday, Thursday, Friday, Saturday, Sunday.
explain: Sunday is also part of the weekend. In many places it is a day of rest, or a day for going to church. «His dad plays a game with him on Sunday mornings» shows that Sunday can be a day for fun at home.
explain: The words around Sunday give you clues. Words such as «on», «on Sundays» and «next Sunday» tell you when something happens. «Ollie tried out a word at Sunday dinner» tells you the dinner was on Sunday.
explain: Sunday is a noun, so you can make it plural: Sundays. The phrase «Sunday best» means your smartest clothes, not a day. Always check which meaning fits the sentence.
fact: Sunday is a day of the week. It comes after Saturday and before Monday.
fact: A week has 7 days. If Monday is day 1, then Sunday is day 7.
fact: Sunday is part of the weekend, and in many places it is a day of rest or going to church.
fact: Some calendars count Sunday as the first day of the week, and others count it as the last.
fact: «Sunday best» means your smartest clothes.
exercise: Which day comes straight after Saturday? | Friday | Tuesday | *Sunday | Monday
exercise: If Monday is day 1 of the week, which number is Sunday? | 5 | 6 | *7 | 8
exercise: «Sunday best» means what? | *Smartest clothes | A kind of Sunday dinner | A day of rest | Seven days in a row
test: What does «next Sunday» mean? | *The Sunday coming after this one | The Sunday that has already passed | A type of clothes | Every day of the week
test: Which word is the day that comes before Monday? | Saturday | Friday | Wednesday | *Sunday
exam: Write the plural of Sunday. | Sundaies | Sundayes | *Sundays | Sundayies
